INTERPRETATION
Write k=2K, q=2Q, and h=K-(2Q+1).  The previously unresolved wall band is
Q>=1, 0<=h<=3Q-2, and 0<=Y<=2Q+1+h.  Y=0 has zero kernel margin by
definition.  For Y>=1, the nine truncated-binomial hinges in the
three-image Kac-Walton formula have exactly the 23 feasible integer
activation masks listed above.

For 22 masks, the program writes the kernel margin identically as a
nonnegative rational combination of products, of total degree at most
four, of the fourteen nonnegative affine chamber generators.  Z3 only
synthesizes the rational coefficients.  Boost arbitrary-precision rational
arithmetic independently checks every coefficient is nonnegative and
reconstructs every polynomial coefficient of the margin exactly.

Mask 53 is handled without solver synthesis.  Put
a=Y-2Q and b=2Q+a-2h-3.  Its constraints give a,b>=0 and a-b odd.
The four exhaustive cases a=0, b=0, b>a, and a>b have the four affine
parity-cone substitutions checked above.  The program verifies that every
substitution stays inside mask 53 and that every pulled-back margin
coefficient is nonnegative.

